{"name":"Burning Brier","hex":"#884736","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"burning","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of burn"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["So hot as to seem to burn (something).","Feeling very hot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burning"},{"term":"brier","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of briar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brier"}],"entries":[{"title":"Combustion","blocks":[{"text":"Combustion, or burning, is a high-temperature exothermic redox chemical reaction between a fuel and an oxidant, usually atmospheric oxygen, that produces oxidized, often gaseous products, in a mixture termed as smoke. Combustion does not always result in fire, because a flame is only visible when substances undergoing combustion vaporize, but when it does, a flame is a characteristic indicator of the reaction. While activation energy must be supplied to initiate combustion, the heat from a flame may provide enough energy to make the reaction self-sustaining. The study of combustion is known as combustion science."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Fire%2C_Fireplace%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg/330px-Fire%2C_Fireplace%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Combustion"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Regenerative_thermal_oxidizer.jpg/500px-Regenerative_thermal_oxidizer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Regenerative_thermal_oxidizer.jpg/1280px-Regenerative_thermal_oxidizer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Regenerative_thermal_oxidizer.jpg/500px-Regenerative_thermal_oxidizer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Air pollution abatement equipment provides combustion control for industrial processes.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARegenerative_thermal_oxidizer.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Microgravity_Burning.jpg/500px-Microgravity_Burning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Microgravity_Burning.jpg/1280px-Microgravity_Burning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Microgravity_Burning.jpg/500px-Microgravity_Burning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Colourized gray-scale composite image of the individual frames from a video of a backlit fuel droplet burning in microgravity","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMicrogravity_Burning.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Zoom_lunette_ardente.jpg/500px-Zoom_lunette_ardente.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Zoom_lunette_ardente.jpg/500px-Zoom_lunette_ardente.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Antoine Lavoisier conducting an experiment related to combustion generated by amplified sunlight","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZoom_lunette_ardente.jpg"}],"sounds":{"burning":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/41/En-us-burning.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/41/En-us-burning.ogg/En-us-burning.ogg.mp3"}]}}}